.TH JBMC "1" "March 1, 2026" "jbmc-6.10.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
jbmc \- Bounded model checker for Java bytecode
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B jbmc
.RI [ options ]
.I method-name
.br
.B jbmc
.RI [ options ]
.I class-name
.br
.B jbmc
.RI [ options ]
.BI \-jar " jarfile"
.br
.B jbmc
.RI [ options ]
.BI \-\-gb " goto-binary"
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBjbmc\fR is a bounded model checker for Java programs.  It verifies Java
bytecode by converting it into an intermediate GOTO representation and then
performing symbolic execution up to a given bound.  It can check
user-specified assertions, uncaught exceptions, and a range of runtime
properties such as array bounds and null pointer dereferences.
.PP
\fBjbmc\fR can read Java class files, JAR archives, or pre-compiled GOTO
binaries.  It shares the same verification back-end as \fBcbmc\fR(1) but
uses a Java bytecode front-end.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-classpath\fR \fIdirs/jars\fR, \fB\-cp\fR \fIdirs/jars\fR,
\fB\-\-classpath\fR \fIdirs/jars\fR
Set the class search path using a colon-separated list of directories and
JAR archives to search for class files.
.TP
\fB\-\-main\-class\fR \fIclass\-name\fR
Set the name of the main class.  When loading a JAR file, this overrides
the Main-Class entry in the JAR manifest.
.TP
\fB\-\-function\fR \fIname\fR
Use the method \fIname\fR as the entry point instead of
\fBpublic static void main(String[])\fR.  The name should be a fully
qualified method descriptor, e.g., \fI'mypackage.Myclass.foo:(I)Z'\fR.
.SS "Analysis options:"
.TP
\fB\-\-show\-properties\fR
List all properties in the program without running the analysis.
.TP
\fB\-\-symex\-coverage\-report\fR \fIfile\fR
Generate a Cobertura XML coverage report in \fIfile\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-property\fR \fIid\fR
Only check the property with the given \fIid\fR.  Use
\fB\-\-show\-properties\fR to list available identifiers.
.TP
\fB\-\-trace\fR
Print a counterexample trace for each failed property.
.TP
\fB\-\-stop\-on\-fail\fR
Stop the analysis as soon as the first property violation is found.
Implies \fB\-\-trace\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-localize\-faults\fR
Attempt to identify the most likely source of a property violation
(experimental).
.TP
\fB\-\-validate\-trace\fR
Verify that the structure of the counterexample trace matches expected
invariants (experimental, Java only).
.SS "Platform options:"
.TP
\fB\-\-arch\fR \fIarch\fR
Set analysis architecture, which defaults to the host architecture. Use one of:
\fBalpha\fR, \fBarm\fR, \fBarm64\fR, \fBarmel\fR, \fBarmhf\fR, \fBhppa\fR,
\fBi386\fR, \fBia64\fR,
\fBmips\fR, \fBmips64\fR, \fBmips64el\fR, \fBmipsel\fR, \fBmipsn32\fR,
\fBmipsn32el\fR, \fBpowerpc\fR, \fBppc64\fR, \fBppc64le\fR, \fBriscv64\fR,
\fBs390\fR,
\fBs390x\fR, \fBsh4\fR, \fBsparc\fR, \fBsparc64\fR, \fBv850\fR, \fBx32\fR,
\fBx86_64\fR, or
\fBnone\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-os\fR \fIos\fR
Set analysis operating system, which defaults to the host operating system. Use
one of: \fBfreebsd\fR, \fBlinux\fR, \fBmacos\fR, \fBnetbsd\fR, \fBopenbsd\fR,
\fBsolaris\fR, \fBhurd\fR, or \fBwindows\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-i386\-linux\fR, \fB\-\-i386\-win32\fR, \fB\-\-i386\-macos\fR,
\fB\-\-ppc\-macos\fR, \fB\-\-win32\fR, \fB\-\-winx64\fR
Set analysis architecture and operating system.
.TP
\fB\-\-LP64\fR, \fB\-\-ILP64\fR, \fB\-\-LLP64\fR, \fB\-\-ILP32\fR,
\fB\-\-LP32\fR
Set width of int, long and pointers, but don't override default architecture and
operating system.
.TP
\fB\-\-16\fR, \fB\-\-32\fR, \fB\-\-64\fR
Equivalent to \fB\-\-LP32\fR, \fB\-\-ILP32\fR, \fB\-\-LP64\fR (on Windows:
\fB\-\-LLP64\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-little\-endian\fR
allow little\-endian word\-byte conversions
.TP
\fB\-\-big\-endian\fR
allow big\-endian word\-byte conversions
.TP
\fB\-\-gcc\fR
use GCC as preprocessor
.SS "Program representations:"
.TP
\fB\-\-show\-parse\-tree\fR
Display the parse tree of the loaded bytecode.
.TP
\fB\-\-show\-symbol\-table\fR
Display the symbol table, listing all variables, methods, and types.
.TP
\fB\-\-list\-symbols\fR
List symbols with their type information.
.TP
\fB\-\-show\-goto\-functions\fR
Display the GOTO program instructions for all loaded methods.
.TP
\fB\-\-list\-goto\-functions\fR
List the names of all loaded methods without showing their bodies.
.TP
\fB\-\-drop\-unused\-functions\fR
Remove methods that are trivially unreachable from the entry point.
.TP
\fB\-\-show\-class\-hierarchy\fR
Display the Java class inheritance hierarchy.
.SS "Program instrumentation options:"
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-assertions\fR
Ignore all user-written assertions.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-assumptions\fR
Ignore all assumptions.
.TP
\fB\-\-mm\fR \fIMM\fR
Set the memory consistency model for concurrent programs.
.TP
\fB\-\-reachability\-slice\fR
Remove instructions that cannot appear on any trace from the entry
point to a property.
.TP
\fB\-\-reachability\-slice\-fb\fR
Remove instructions that cannot appear on any trace from the entry
point \fIthrough\fR a property (forward-backward slicing).
.TP
\fB\-\-full\-slice\fR
Remove all instructions that do not affect any assertion (experimental).
.SS "Java Bytecode frontend options:"
.TP
\fB\-\-disable\-uncaught\-exception\-check\fR
ignore uncaught exceptions and errors
.TP
\fB\-\-throw\-assertion\-error\fR
Throw java.lang.AssertionError on violated
\fBassert\fR statements instead of failing
at the location of the \fBassert\fR statement.
.TP
\fB\-\-throw\-runtime\-exceptions\fR
Make implicit runtime exceptions explicit.
.TP
\fB\-\-assert\-no\-exceptions\-thrown\fR
Transform \fBthrow\fR instructions into \fBassert FALSE\fR
followed by \fBassume FALSE\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-nondet\-array\-length\fR \fIN\fR
Limit nondet (e.g. input) array size to at most \fIN\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-nondet\-tree\-depth\fR \fIN\fR
Limit size of nondet (e.g. input) object tree;
at level \fIN\fR references are set to \fBnull\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-java\-assume\-inputs\-non\-null\fR
Never initialize reference-typed parameter to the
entry point with \fBnull\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-java\-assume\-inputs\-interval\fR [\fIL\fR:\fIU\fR] or [\fIL\fR:] or
[:\fIU\fR]
Force numerical primitive-typed inputs (\fBbyte\fR, \fBshort\fR, \fBint\fR,
\fBlong\fR, \fBfloat\fR, \fBdouble\fR) to be initialized within the given range;
lower bound \fIL\fR and upper bound \fIU\fR must be integers; does not work for
arrays.
.TP
\fB\-\-java\-assume\-inputs\-integral\fR
Force float and double inputs to have integer values;
does not work for arrays;
.TP
\fB\-\-java\-max\-vla\-length\fR \fIN\fR
Limit the length of user\-code\-created arrays to \fIN\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-java\-cp\-include\-files\fR \fIr\fR
Regular expression or JSON list of files to load
(with '@' prefix).
.TP
\fB\-\-java\-load\-class\fR \fICLASS\fR
Also load code from class \fICLASS\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-java\-no\-load\-class\fR \fICLASS\fR
Never load code from class \fICLASS\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-ignore\-manifest\-main\-class\fR
Ignore Main\-Class entries in JAR manifest files.
If this option is specified and the options
\fB\-\-function\fR and \fB\-\-main\-class\fR are not, we can be
certain that all classes in the JAR file are
loaded.
.TP
\fB\-\-context\-include\fR \fIi\fR, \fB\-\-context\-exclude\fR \fIe\fR
Only analyze code matching specification \fIi\fR that
does not match specification \fIe\fR, if
\fB\-\-context\-exclude\fR \fIe\fR is also used.
All other methods are excluded, i.e., we load their
signatures and meta\-information, but not their
bodies.
A specification is any prefix of a package, class
or method name, e.g. "org.cprover." or
"org.cprover.MyClass." or
"org.cprover.MyClass.methodToStub:(I)Z".
These options can be given multiple times.
The default for context\-include is 'all
included'; default for context\-exclude is
\&'nothing excluded'.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-lazy\-methods\fR
Load and translate all methods given on
the command line and in \fB\-\-classpath\fR
Default is to load methods that appear to be
reachable from the \fB\-\-function\fR entry point
or main class.
Note that \fB\-\-show\-symbol\-table\fR, \fB\-\-show\-goto\-functions\fR
and \fB\-\-show\-properties\fR output are restricted to
loaded methods by default.
.TP
\fB\-\-lazy\-methods\-extra\-entry\-point\fR \fIMETHODNAME\fR
Treat \fIMETHODNAME\fR as a possible program entry
point for the purpose of lazy method loading.
\fIMETHODNAME\fR can be a regular expression that will be matched
against all symbols. If missing, a \fBjava::\fR prefix
will be added. If no descriptor is found, all
overloads of a method will also be added.
.TP
\fB\-\-static\-values\fR \fIf\fR
Load initial values of static fields from the given
JSON file. We assign static fields to these values
instead of calling the normal static initializer
(clinit) method.
The argument can be a relative or absolute path to
the file.
.TP
\fB\-\-java\-lift\-clinit\-calls\fR
Lifts clinit calls in function bodies to the top of the
function. This may reduce the overall cost of static
initialisation, but may be unsound if there are
cyclic dependencies between static initializers due
to potentially changing their order of execution,
or if static initializers have side\-effects such as
updating another class' static field.
.TP
\fB\-\-java\-threading\fR
enable java multi\-threading support (experimental)
.TP
\fB\-\-java\-unwind\-enum\-static\fR
unwind loops in static initialization of enums
.TP
\fB\-\-symex\-driven\-lazy\-loading\fR
only load functions when first entered by symbolic
execution. Note that \fB\-\-show\-symbol\-table\fR,
\fB\-\-show\-goto\-functions\fR/properties output
will be restricted to loaded methods in this case,
and only output after the symex phase.
.SS "Semantic transformations:"
.TP
\fB\-\-nondet\-static\fR
Initialize all variables with static lifetime to non-deterministic
values instead of their declared initializers.
.SS "BMC options:"
.TP
\fB\-\-paths\fR [\fIstrategy\fR]
Explore execution paths one at a time instead of merging them.
Use \fB\-\-show\-symex\-strategies\fR to list available strategies.
.TP
\fB\-\-show\-symex\-strategies\fR
List available path exploration strategies for use with \fB\-\-paths\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-show\-goto\-symex\-steps\fR
Print each step that symbolic execution takes, including diagnostic
information about the call stack and guard size.
.TP
\fB\-\-show\-points\-to\-sets\fR
Print points-to sets computed during pointer dereference resolution.
Requires \fB\-\-json\-ui\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-program\-only\fR
Print the program expression (SSA equations) without solving.
.TP
\fB\-\-show\-byte\-ops\fR
Print all byte-extract and byte-update operations in the formula.
.TP
\fB\-\-depth\fR \fInr\fR
Limit search depth to \fInr\fR instructions on any single execution path.
When the depth limit is reached, any remaining paths are cut short.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-field\-sensitivity\-array\-size\fR \fIM\fR
Apply field sensitivity (tracking individual elements) to arrays of at
most \fIM\fR elements.  The default is 64.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-array\-field\-sensitivity\fR
Disable field sensitivity for arrays entirely.  Equivalent to
\fB\-\-max\-field\-sensitivity\-array\-size\fR \fI0\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-show\-loops\fR
List all loops in the program with their identifiers.
.TP
\fB\-\-unwind\fR \fInr\fR
Unwind all loops at most \fInr\fR times.
.TP
\fB\-\-unwindset\fR [\fIT\fR:]\fIL\fR:\fIB\fR,...
Set a per-loop unwinding bound: unwind loop \fIL\fR at most \fIB\fR times,
optionally restricted to thread \fIT\fR.  Use \fB\-\-show\-loops\fR to obtain
loop IDs.
.TP
\fB\-\-incremental\-loop\fR \fIL\fR
Check properties after each unwinding of loop \fIL\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-unwind\-min\fR \fInr\fR
When using \fB\-\-incremental\-loop\fR, start checking after \fInr\fR
unwindings.
.TP
\fB\-\-unwind\-max\fR \fInr\fR
When using \fB\-\-incremental\-loop\fR, stop after \fInr\fR unwindings.
.TP
\fB\-\-ignore\-properties\-before\-unwind\-min\fR
Do not check properties before \fB\-\-unwind\-min\fR is reached.
.TP
\fB\-\-show\-vcc\fR
Print the verification conditions without solving them.
.TP
\fB\-\-slice\-formula\fR
Remove assignments from the formula that do not affect any property.
.TP
\fB\-\-unwinding\-assertions\fR
Generate assertions that check whether the loop unwinding bound is
sufficient.  Enabled by default.  Overrides \fB\-\-no\-unwinding\-assertions\fR
when both are given.  Cannot be used with \fB\-\-cover\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-unwinding\-assertions\fR
Do not generate unwinding assertions.
.TP
\fB\-\-partial\-loops\fR
Permit execution paths that exit a loop before the loop condition
becomes false.  Such paths may be spurious, resulting in false alarms.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-self\-loops\-to\-assumptions\fR
Do not simplify self-loops such as \fBwhile(1){}\fR to
\fBassume(false)\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-symex\-complexity\-limit\fR \fIN\fR
Abandon execution paths whose complexity exceeds \fIN\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-symex\-complexity\-failed\-child\-loops\-limit\fR \fIN\fR
Blacklist a loop after \fIN\fR of its child branches have been abandoned
due to complexity violations.
.TP
\fB\-\-graphml\-witness\fR \fIfilename\fR
Write a verification witness in GraphML format to \fIfilename\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-symex\-cache\-dereferences\fR
Cache the results of repeated pointer dereferences during symbolic
execution.
.SS "Backend options:"
.TP
\fB\-\-object\-bits\fR \fIn\fR
Set the number of bits used for object addresses in the pointer model.
.TP
\fB\-\-sat\-solver\fR \fIsolver\fR
Use the specified SAT solver.
.TP
\fB\-\-external\-sat\-solver\fR \fIcmd\fR
Invoke \fIcmd\fR as an external SAT solver process.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-sat\-preprocessor\fR
Disable the SAT solver's built-in simplifier.
.TP
\fB\-\-dimacs\fR
Output the formula in DIMACS CNF format instead of solving it.
.TP
\fB\-\-beautify\fR
Attempt to produce a more readable counterexample using a greedy
heuristic.
.TP
\fB\-\-smt2\fR
Use the default SMT2 solver (Z3).
.TP
\fB\-\-smt1\fR
Use the default SMT1 solver (obsolete).
.TP
\fB\-\-bitwuzla\fR
Use Bitwuzla as the SMT solver.
.TP
\fB\-\-boolector\fR
Use Boolector as the SMT solver.
.TP
\fB\-\-cprover\-smt2\fR
Use the CProver built-in SMT2 solver.
.TP
\fB\-\-cvc5\fR
Use CVC5 as the SMT solver.
.TP
\fB\-\-mathsat\fR
Use MathSAT as the SMT solver.
.TP
\fB\-\-yices\fR
Use Yices as the SMT solver.
.TP
\fB\-\-z3\fR
Use Z3 as the SMT solver.
.TP
\fB\-\-fpa\fR
Use the theory of floating-point arithmetic in the SMT encoding.
.TP
\fB\-\-external\-smt2\-solver\fR \fIcmd\fR
Invoke \fIcmd\fR as an external SMT2 solver process.
.TP
\fB\-\-refine\fR
Use counterexample-guided abstraction refinement (experimental).
.TP
\fB\-\-refine\-arrays\fR
Use abstraction refinement for arrays only.
.TP
\fB\-\-refine\-arithmetic\fR
Use abstraction refinement for arithmetic expressions only.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-node\-refinement\fR \fIN\fR
Limit the number of refinement iterations for arithmetic expressions.
.TP
\fB\-\-incremental\-smt2\-solver\fR \fIcmd\fR
Use the incremental SMT backend, invoking \fIcmd\fR as the solver.
The solver must accept incremental SMTlib v2.6 input on standard input
and support the QF_AUFBV logic.
.TP
\fB\-\-outfile\fR \fIfilename\fR
Write the generated formula to \fIfilename\fR instead of solving it.
.TP
\fB\-\-dump\-smt\-formula\fR \fIfilename\fR
Write the SMT formula to \fIfilename\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-write\-solver\-stats\-to\fR \fIjson\-file\fR
Write solver query complexity statistics to \fIjson\-file\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-refine\-strings\fR
Disable string refinement.
.TP
\fB\-\-string\-printable\fR
Restrict non-deterministic strings to printable characters.
.TP
\fB\-\-string\-non\-empty\fR
Restrict non-deterministic strings to be non-empty (experimental).
.TP
\fB\-\-string\-input\-value\fR \fIst\fR
Restrict non-null strings to the fixed value \fIst\fR.  May be given
multiple times to specify several possible values.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-nondet\-string\-length\fR \fIn\fR
Limit the length of non-deterministic strings to \fIn\fR.  The default
is 67108863.  Values higher than this do not work with \fB\-\-trace\fR or
\fB\-\-validate\-trace\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-arrays\-uf\-never\fR
Never encode arrays as uninterpreted functions.
.TP
\fB\-\-arrays\-uf\-always\fR
Always encode arrays as uninterpreted functions.
.SS "Other options:"
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
Print version information and exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-xml\-ui\fR
Produce output in XML format.
.TP
\fB\-\-xml\-interface\fR
Enable the bi-directional XML interface.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\-ui\fR
Produce output in JSON format.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\-interface\fR
Enable the bi-directional JSON interface.
.TP
\fB\-\-validate\-goto\-model\fR
Run additional well-formedness checks on the GOTO program.
.TP
\fB\-\-validate\-ssa\-equation\fR
Run additional well-formedness checks on the SSA representation.
.TP
\fB\-\-trace\-json\-extended\fR
Include the \fBrawLhs\fR property in JSON trace output.
.TP
\fB\-\-trace\-show\-function\-calls\fR
Include function call and return events in plain-text traces.
.TP
\fB\-\-trace\-show\-code\fR
Include the original source code in plain-text traces.
.TP
\fB\-\-trace\-hex\fR
Display values in hexadecimal in plain-text traces.
.TP
\fB\-\-compact\-trace\fR
Produce a compact counterexample trace.
.TP
\fB\-\-stack\-trace\fR
Produce only a stack trace for counterexamples.
.TP
\fB\-\-flush\fR
Flush every line of output immediately.
.TP
\fB\-\-verbosity\fR \fIN\fR
Set the verbosity level to \fIN\fR (default: 6).
.TP
\fB\-\-timestamp\fR [\fBmonotonic\fR|\fBwall\fR]
Print microsecond-precision timestamps.
\fBmonotonic\fR: timestamps increase monotonically.
\fBwall\fR: ISO\-8601 wall-clock timestamps.
.SH EXAMPLES
Verify a Java class (entry point is \fBmain\fR):
.IP
.B jbmc MyClass
.PP
Verify a JAR file:
.IP
.B jbmc \-jar app.jar
.PP
Verify a specific method by its fully qualified descriptor:
.IP
.B jbmc \(aqcom.example.Foo.bar:(I)Z\(aq
.PP
Verify with a loop unwinding bound:
.IP
.B jbmc \-\-unwind 10 MyClass
.PP
Set the classpath and main class for a JAR:
.IP
.B jbmc \-jar app.jar \-\-main\-class com.example.Main \-\-classpath lib/
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All properties verified successfully.
.TP
.B 1
Usage error: invalid or conflicting command line options.
.TP
.B 2
Parse error: an input file could not be parsed.
.TP
.B 6
An internal error or unhandled exception occurred.
.TP
.B 10
One or more properties were violated.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TMPDIR
All CProver tools honor this variable when creating temporary files and
directories.
.SH BUGS
If you encounter a problem please create an issue at
.B https://github.com/diffblue/cbmc/issues
